  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Around the world",
  "description": "A trick where the foot goes all the way round the ball while it is in the air. Everyone has a ball. Put out four cones in a square as stations, one for each step of the trick ladder. Everyone starts at station 1, and the coach shows the trick first.\n\nStation 1: lift the ball onto your instep and hold it still there, with the foot a little off the ground, for three seconds. Station 2: flick the ball up a little, let it bounce once while your foot circles round it, and catch it on the instep again. Station 3: the same without the bounce. Station 4: do the trick in both directions, with both feet one after the other, or with two circles round the ball.\n\nManage the trick three times in a row and you move on to the next station. Anyone who has cleared station 4 makes up a trick of their own or goes back to help someone who is still at station 1. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Lift the ball straight up and high enough – about waist height."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Quick foot: start the circle as soon as the ball leaves your foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Standing leg slightly bent and arms out for balance."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Practise as much with your left foot as with your right."
    }
  ],
